Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||01-18-2001||01:55 PM||||I was under the car the otherday and it looks like the steering dampner is a shell (rusted out and quite ugly).  This causes steering wander right!<P>I will replace it soon when i have some cash just wondering.<P>Also does any one know the secret to removing used ashtray covers or installing them.  I have broke some in the past and want to replace them.<P>Next the throttle cable seems to have stretched.  When the padle is depressed all the way the throttle only rotates 80% of the way to the stop point (where it hits metal)<BR>There is slack in the cable too.  Any way to get rid of this?<P>thanks<BR>ps.  87 duke<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<p>[This message has been edited by kinboyatuwo (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-18-2001||07:10 PM||||I take it you must be asking about the ash tray doors.<P>On the underside of the doors, you'll see that they pivot on little ears.  There is a slot in the "ears", and just carefully pry them away, a little at a time, going from one side to the other.  After they come off, just disconnect the hold down spring and slide the door out.<P>Just last night I had to fix one of mine, and broke one of the ears off in the process of removing it.  Super glue held it back in place perfectly.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
